  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TJN Tax Shift Towards global justice and financial transparency</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project support three elements- research and analyses; support to national and regional advocacy and international communication and advocacy. 

Outcome 1) Target groups have an increased understanding of the harm of financial secrecy, illicit financial flows and corporate tax havenry at a national, regional and global level.
Outcome 2) Target groups have increased capacity with the tools and skills to address the harm being caused.
Outcome 3) Countries take unilateral and multilateral steps to adopt the ABC policy measures of tax transparency, Automatic information exchange, public registers of Beneficial ownership, public Country-by-country reporting, including through an international convention and globally inclusive rule setting.
Outcome 4) Global human rights standards and treaties explicitly include tax justice requirements and hold governments accountable to them.</narrative>
  </description>
